{"change_summary":"Documented the intentional shrimp molt-stress pressure blend as sensitivity coefficients in `update_molt_stress` instead of a normalized partition, extended structured tracing to emit `animal.molt_readiness` and `animal.failed_molt_accum` alongside existing molt stress, and added a daily-shrimp trace regression that exercises a forced failed molt so the multi-day cascade state is observable. I also synchronized nitrification alkalinity defaults across `ProcessParams::default()`, the `tank_data` preset default function, the shipped `process/default.toml`, and scenario materialization by sourcing the preset-side default from `NITRIFICATION_ALK_MEQ_PER_MG_N` and adding data/scenario regressions that lock the constant alignment down.","outstanding_risks":[],"steps":[{"description":"Inspected the pending amendment paths in shrimp stress blending, tracing, and process preset defaults to confirm which gaps still existed on the current branch.","order":1,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Updated shrimp tracing and diagnostics by documenting the oversubscribed pressure blend design and exposing `molt_readiness` plus `failed_molt_accum` in the traced pool set.","order":2,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Synchronized the nitrification alkalinity constant across runtime defaults, preset parsing, shipped process data, and scenario materialization, then added regression coverage for the preset/runtime contract.","order":3,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Ran formatting plus targeted and full-suite validation across `tank_core`, `tank_data`, and `tank_scenarios` to verify the pending amendments end to end.","order":4,"status":"completed"}],"validation_evidence":["cargo fmt --all","cargo test -p tank_core --test tracing -- --nocapture","cargo test -p tank_core --test nitrification_alkalinity -- --nocapture","cargo test -p tank_data -- --nocapture","cargo test -p tank_scenarios -- --nocapture","cargo test -p tank_core -- --nocapture"]}